2. Authentication flow

This is probably the most important part of the project.

When someone logs in:

User enters email/password
        ↓
supabase.auth.signInWithPassword()
        ↓
Supabase Auth
        ↓
auth.users
        ↓
profiles
        ↓
Check role
        ↓
student / teacher / admin
        ↓
Open correct dashboard

The authentication module calls:

sb.auth.signInWithPassword({
    email,
    password
});

Then it loads the user's profile from:

profiles

using the authenticated user's ID.

It checks:

profile exists
profile.is_active === true
role is correct

Then:

window.LFS_CURRENT_PROFILE = profile;

is set.

Finally:

goScreen('dash-' + profile.role);

routes the user.

This is implemented in supabase-auth.js.

