4. Why profiles is important

profiles is basically the application's identity table.

For example:

profiles
--------------------------------
id
full_name
email
role
is_active
phone
avatar_url
...

The critical relationship is:

auth.users.id
      =
profiles.id

So:

Supabase Auth tells us who logged in.

profiles tells us who that person is inside LFS.

5. Student dashboard data flow

This was one of the biggest things we fixed.

The student dashboard does not just use a hardcoded name anymore.

The intended relationship is:

auth.users
    │
    ▼
profiles
    │
    ▼
students
    │
    ▼
student_class_assignments
    │
    ▼
class_sections
    │
    ▼
classes

The current student-profile-sync.js explicitly documents this relationship.

Example

Suppose:

auth.users.id = ABC

Then:

profiles.id = ABC
students.id = ABC

Then:

student_class_assignments.student_id = ABC

Then:

student_class_assignments.class_section_id
        ↓
class_sections.id

Then:

class_sections.class_id
        ↓
classes.id

And finally we can obtain:

Class 11
Section A
Roll 23
6. How the student's name appears

student-profile-sync.js gets:

profile.full_name

and eventually calls:

applyStudentData(cached);

The function updates:

#dash-student-name
#dash-student-info

and also:

pfName
pfRole
pfAvatar

It also updates the digital ID card.

So one database value can populate multiple UI locations.

The current implementation does this in applyStudentData().

