8. Student sync fallback system

This is important for debugging.

If there is no session:

No active session

the module doesn't try to query student data.

It displays:

Hi, Student
Class not assigned
--

If the profile exists but the students record doesn't:

Name still comes from profiles

If the class assignment doesn't exist:

Name still appears
Class not assigned

This was deliberately done so one missing database relationship doesn't completely destroy the dashboard.

The current code logs each stage and caches partial data.

9. Supabase client problem we had

We previously had:

Supabase client is not initialized

The reason was that different modules expected different global variables.

We changed the authentication layer so the client is exposed through:

window.LFS_SUPABASE_CLIENT
window.LFS_SUPABASE
window.LFS_SUPABASE_READY

Student sync waits for:

window.LFS_SUPABASE_READY

before querying the database.

This is why you should not randomly create another Supabase client in another JS file.

Use the existing client.

10. Registration system

A student/teacher can create an account.

The registration function calls:

sb.auth.signUp(...)

with metadata such as:

full_name
requested_role
class_section_id
roll_number
employee_id

The account is then supposed to go through approval.

The intended architecture is:

Register
   ↓
auth.users
   ↓
registration_requests
   ↓
pending
   ↓
Admin reviews
   ↓
Approve / Reject
11. Registration approval

registration-approval.js handles the database operations.

It provides:

getPendingRegistrationRequests()
getMyNotifications()
markNotificationRead()
reviewRegistrationRequest()
routeRegistrationRequest()

The pending request query uses:

registration_requests

with:

status = pending

and joins:

class_sections
classes

The approval operation uses the database RPC:

review_registration_request

rather than directly modifying several tables from the frontend.

12. Admin approval UI

registration-review-ui.js creates the admin/teacher registration-review interface dynamically.

It:

Checks the logged-in profile.
Gets pending requests.
Filters them based on role.
Displays the request.
Allows:
Approve
Reject
Calls the approval RPC.
Refreshes the UI.

For students, teachers can see requests associated with their class, while admins can see all applicable requests.

The module also subscribes to Supabase realtime changes on:

notifications
registration_requests

so the UI can refresh when those tables change.

13. Friend registration problem

We had a situation where your friend's confirmed account wasn't appearing in Student Approval.

The important distinction is:

Email confirmed

does NOT automatically mean:

LFS approved

There are separate layers:

Supabase Auth account
        ↓
registration request
        ↓
school approval
        ↓
active profile
        ↓
student record

We added a database trigger so new student/teacher Auth registrations can create a registration_requests row automatically.

So if your friend registers correctly through the LFS registration UI, the expected path is:

Auth user
   ↓
registration_requests
   ↓
pending
   ↓
Admin sees request
