19. Why index.html is dangerous

This is probably the most important developer warning.

index.html is enormous and contains:

HTML
CSS
JavaScript
Base64 images
demo data
UI logic
navigation logic

all in one file.

We've previously had accidental syntax problems such as:

<script> without </script>

and:

missing }

which caused errors like:

Unexpected token 'async'

and:

JSX element script has no corresponding closing tag

Those errors caused many apparently unrelated buttons to stop working.

Therefore:

Never replace the entire index.html just to fix one feature.

Make a small change.

Test.

Then commit.

20. Why some buttons stopped working

Many of the buttons are controlled by JavaScript functions defined inside the giant index.html.

If one syntax error occurs early in the script:

JavaScript stops parsing
        ↓
functions below it don't exist
        ↓
buttons call undefined functions
        ↓
many buttons appear broken

So:

One syntax error can look like 20 different UI bugs.

That's why we previously got stuck in the cycle:

fix error
 ↓
another error
 ↓
fix another error
 ↓
buttons disappear
 ↓
fix buttons
 ↓
new syntax error

The correct approach is to fix syntax first, then functionality.

21. Debugging strategy for your friend

Tell him to use this order:

Step 1 — Console

Open:

F12 → Console

Find the first red error.

Ignore the 30 errors underneath it initially.

Fix the first one.

Reload.

Step 2 — Syntax

Before debugging Supabase:

Check JS syntax

If the browser says:

Unexpected token
Unexpected identifier
Expected }
Expected <
Unexpected async

don't touch the database.

Fix JavaScript first.

Step 3 — Authentication

Check:

auth.users

Then:

profiles

Then:

is_active
role
Step 4 — Student data

Check:

students
student_class_assignments
class_sections
classes

in that order.

Step 5 — UI

Only after the database query works:

applyStudentData()

should be investigated.

